    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Nice's second dog beach alongside Lenval, Carras is a pebble beach that has welcomed dogs since 2008. It sits at the western end of the Promenade des Anglais, near the airport and the harbour of the same name.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Unlike many beaches in the area that close to dogs in summer, Carras stays open year-round, on a leash. Dogs can swim and play together in this dedicated space.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: combined with the Lenval beach a bit further east, this beach makes Nice one of the most dog-friendly cities on the French Riviera.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The neighbourhood is more residential than central Nice, handy if you're after a quieter moment than the heart of the Promenade des Anglais.</p>
